{#
  Scopes the cross-document view transitions this theme opts into
  (@view-transition in theme.source.css) to catalog-internal navigations. Without
  it every navigation crossfades the whole viewport, and leaving a light listing
  for the dark home blends the two snapshots into a grey wash.

  A module script is late enough for `pageswap` (it fires on user navigation) and
  avoids the parser-blocking script in the head that `pagereveal` would demand.

  The pseudo-element rules are inline rather than in theme.source.css on purpose:
  the browser starts the transition at the incoming document's FIRST render, and
  at that point the stylesheet is still loading (it is preloaded and swapped in by
  onload). Critical-CSS extraction cannot rescue them either — it keeps the rules
  whose selectors match the rendered DOM, and a ::view-transition pseudo never
  appears there. Left in the stylesheet they simply do not apply to the animation
  they are meant to shape.
#}
<style>
    /* Hold the chrome still: show the incoming snapshot alone, since fading
       between two identical images still dips through a blend. */
    ::view-transition-group(obsidian-header),
    ::view-transition-group(obsidian-footer) { animation: none; }
    ::view-transition-image-pair(obsidian-header),
    ::view-transition-image-pair(obsidian-footer) { isolation: auto; }
    ::view-transition-old(obsidian-header),
    ::view-transition-old(obsidian-footer) { display: none; }
    ::view-transition-new(obsidian-header),
    ::view-transition-new(obsidian-footer) { animation: none; mix-blend-mode: normal; }

    /* The outgoing page holds until the incoming one paints over it. Fading it
       out on a timer leaves the viewport blank whenever the new document is not
       ready yet, which is what shows the header floating over nothing. Normal
       blending, not the default plus-lighter: with the old frame kept opaque,
       adding the two would wash the overlap out. */
    ::view-transition-image-pair(root) { isolation: auto; }
    ::view-transition-old(root) { animation: none; opacity: 1; mix-blend-mode: normal; }
    ::view-transition-new(root) { animation-duration: 220ms; mix-blend-mode: normal; }

    ::view-transition-group(pdp-hero) {
        animation-duration: 320ms;
        animation-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1);
    }

    /* The global reduced-motion blanket cannot reach these pseudos. */
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        ::view-transition-group(*),
        ::view-transition-old(*),
        ::view-transition-new(*) { animation: none !important; }
    }
</style>
<script type="module" src="{{ vite_url('MageObsidian_Storefront::js/viewTransitions') }}"></script>
